    note right of WorkflowAttemptService
        **add_attempt()** validates:
        • attempt.id is globally unique
        • (run_id, attempt_number) pair is unique
        • Raises ValueError with message:
          "Attempt number {N} already exists for run '{id}'."

        **filter_by_run_id()** returns:
        • All attempts for given run_id
        • Sorted by attempt_number (ascending)
    end note

    note right of WorkflowDataPortabilityService
        **export_runs()** and **export_attempts()**:
        • Exports all data if runs/attempts list is None
        • Creates parent directories if needed
        • Returns count of exported items

        **import_runs()** and **import_attempts()**:
        • Validates JSON schema before import
        • Detects duplicate IDs
        • Returns dict with:
          imported, skipped, count, successful, failed
    end note

    note right of GitHubIntegrationService
        **fetch_runs()** and **fetch_run_attempts()**:
        • Primary entry points for GitHub integration
        • Token resolved via priority:
          1. GITHUB_TOKEN env var
          2. secrets/.env file
          3. Interactive prompt
        • Validates token before API call
        • Supports two fetch modes: REST API or gh CLI
        • Returns domain models (WorkflowRun, WorkflowRunAttempt)

        **Timestamp Parsing**:
        • Converts GitHub ISO 8601 strings to UTC datetime
        • Handles Z suffix and timezone-aware strings

        **Data Conversion**:
        • _convert_api_run(): GitHub API → WorkflowRun
        • _convert_api_attempt(): GitHub API → WorkflowRunAttempt
        • Calculates duration from timestamps
        • Validates status and conclusion enums
    end note
}

